                <pb facs="0065" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/848c: Circular
                    telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Diplomatic Representatives in
                        the American Republics</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-07T16:00:00-05:00">December 7, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Hawaii and Manila have been bombed by the Japanese. The President has accordingly
                    ordered that the war plans against Japan be made effective at once. Please
                    notify Foreign Office immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
